# DTF tier manifest: disk-usage-thresholds (artifact-keeper#5191)
# Profile-set: storage.filesystem + storage.disk-thresholds (STORAGE_PATH is a
# 64 MiB tmpfs volume; STORAGE_DISK_WARN_PERCENT=60,
# STORAGE_DISK_BLOCK_PERCENT=80, STORAGE_DISK_CHECK_INTERVAL_SECS=1).
#
# THE BUG
# #5191  The backend did not watch free space on the storage volume. The
#        storage quotas count stored bytes, not the disk; per-repository
#        quotas can add up to more than the volume and proxy caches grow on
#        their own, so with the filesystem backend the first signal of a full
#        disk was a write failing once it was already full (507), with
#        nothing in between. Fix: instance-wide disk usage thresholds measured
#        with statvfs and cached for a few seconds. At the warn threshold a
#        rate-limited warn line and ak_storage_disk_state=1; at the block
#        threshold every write that stores new bytes is refused with
#        403 DISK_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED (reason "Disk Threshold Exceeded",
#        message "server storage nearly full: free disk or add storage ...",
#        OCI: 403 DENIED in the /v2 envelope) before its body is read, while
#        downloads, listing and deletes keep working. Writes resume once the
#        volume is a point below the threshold.
#
# THE PRIMITIVE
#   A helper container (postgres:16-alpine) mounts the same tmpfs volume
#   (ak-dtf<slot>_disk) and grows a fill file to 70 % and then 90 % of the
#   volume, then removes it. The EXIT trap removes it too.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     at 70 %: /api/v1/system/quota .disk.state = warning; a 64 KiB
#             upload still succeeds; a 12 MiB upload whose Content-Length
#             would take the volume past 80 % is refused 403
#             DISK_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED before its body is sent (curl, with
#             Expect: 100-continue, sends less than the body).
#             at 90 %: state = blocked and ak_storage_disk_state = 2; a
#             generic REST PUT, a Maven PUT and a chunked PUT without
#             Content-Length -> 403 DISK_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED with the reason
#             phrase and message; an OCI blob upload start -> 403 DENIED with
#             the message in the /v2 envelope, and so is a chunk PATCH to an
#             OCI upload session opened before the block; the backend log
#             carries the blocked warn line.
#             freed: state = ok, generic and Maven uploads succeed and
#             download.
#   (CONTROL) below the thresholds uploads, downloads, an OCI image push and
#             an upload session start work (50 timed uploads report p50/p95);
#             while blocked generic and Maven downloads (byte-identical), the
#             artifact listing, a DELETE and an OCI blob mount from another image
#             (no bytes written) keep working.
#
# RED: main before #5191 accepts every upload until the volume is actually
# full (no state, no gauge, no refusal): every FIX case fails, every CONTROL
# passes.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 back-to-back API calls.
COVERS="5191"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem storage.disk-thresholds"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
